<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Middle East live: Yemen’s Houthis seize key island in Bab al-Mandab strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff9f1c47937a9add270a6777d9c4a27e8163a0bcdde4101ce34b24df50e6626</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T04:52:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels took over a key island in the Red Sea, completing their push to seize control of the Bab al-Mandab strait area, a local government official and eyewitnesses said on Friday. Perim Island, also known as Mayyun, sits in the middle of the strategic waterway that links Asia to Europe. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels seize strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf8c7df93122b35c71406882d258b1c6d2a5089a50d9c1768d0815ff59614472</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:55:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran--0d8343d16cb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Houthis seized the strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha on Thursday as their offensive against Saudi-backed government forces intensified. Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes over the past 24 hours, the Houthis said, after the Iran-backed group carried out attacks on Saudi territory that wounded dozens of people.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel destroys Hezbollah tunnel network in south Lebanon, triggering 4.1-magnitude tremor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a6bb9b3593391227f5f6eecabdf2d56d51fe2387d7fcb1200be9a995f2000cb</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:50:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake--c28ae45e8d7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake" /><summary type="html">Israel said on Thursday it destroyed key tunnels built by Iran-backed Hezbollah beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, completing what it called operational control of the area. Lebanon reported a massive explosion, while the US Geological Survey recorded a magnitude 4.1 tremor nearby.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran-backed Houthi rebels take strategic port city in Yemen, raising threat to Red Sea shipping</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0633baeda9a328df2f0506df4b10a3238a22ab2d29a9109ea2712f052ae27bf2</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:18:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping--ea40bb9d282d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed Houthi rebel group on Thursday took over Yemen’s port city of Mokha, an area vital to controlling shipping through the Red Sea, Houthi and Yemeni officials said. Mokha is about 80 kilometers (50 miles) from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a waterway that connects the Red Sea and the Gulf of Aden and through which about 12% of the world’s goods are typically shipped. FRANCE 24's Nick Rushworth reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran raises fuel prices for heavy users</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5357c664e52483905c5bd9cd9385266a61ff52afcd5e0f493a3ef0e9109da0cf</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:48:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users--e0de25d0e71c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users" /><summary type="html">The rise of the price of fuel is an issue for both the United States and Iran in this conflict. US president Donald Trump has conceded that prices will not fall before the midterm elections where the US voters could hold him to account. Meanwhile in Iran where many communities have been bombed since February 28th, there's now the added problem of incresing fuel prices. FRANCE 24's Ali al Basha sent this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli-made film about use of AI for mass killing in Gaza gets record ovation at Venice premiere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdb02013af8850a5c503c7585833725bd717c7cf6b250bc46b442271edb37fc7</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:19:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israeli-made-film-about-mass-killings-in-gaza-gets-25-minute-ovation-at-venice-premiere" /><summary type="html">A film documenting Israel's use of artificial intelligence to facilitate the mass killing of Palestinian civilians in the Gaza Strip received a record 25-minute standing ovation at the Venice Film Festival on Thursday. "NAZA" details the brutal Israeli bombardment of the Palestinian territory through anonymous interviews with two dozen whistleblowers from the Israeli military or intelligence services.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>‘I’m spending my savings just to survive’: Iran’s economic crisis fuels new protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7de2f73761cf2f95daf2a094d13d906009a407237144aa1206030abdfdf92e79</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T14:30:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-iran-economic-crisis-protests-war-repression--4c3dfe4a3dc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-iran-economic-crisis-protests-war-repression" /><summary type="html">Despite severe security risks and an ongoing war, retirees, nurses, workers, teachers and students have held sit-ins and protests across Iran since this summer, most often over economic hardship. With prices going up every few hours, salaries and pensions going unpaid for months, and unemployment increasing, our Observers say life is becoming “impossible”.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu visits troops in occupied Syria as Damascus slams 'blatant violation' of sovereignty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e0ea0794324217d20a6815563f8489fe43cfd182f223953cb7e15855ccd080d</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T06:23:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-netanyahu-visits-troops-occupied-syria-damascus-slams-blatant-violation-sovereignty--d21e5845a5ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-netanyahu-visits-troops-occupied-syria-damascus-slams-blatant-violation-sovereignty" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu made a third visit to Israeli troops in an occupied stretch of Syria Wednesday, sparking fresh condemnation from Damascus. Netanyahu repeated his claim that the Iranian government is on the verge of collapse as the US-Israeli war against Iran drags on.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Oil spike past $100 dampens stock prices, fans inflation fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3527c8d4a560195d30ea930022b53c438f9eed2dad90767a78504fa53e63e20</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T02:47:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-stock-prices-drop-as-oil-spike-fans-fears-of-worsening-inflation--87326a3a1a8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-stock-prices-drop-as-oil-spike-fans-fears-of-worsening-inflation" /><summary type="html">As the US and Iran trade air strikes in the vital Strait of Hormuz and Yemen's Houthi rebels step up their campaign against Saudi Arabia, surging oil prices have seen stocks falling across Asia. Investors appear to be holding their breath for the news that the Federal Reserve and other central banks will raise interest rates to tamp down the expected inflation.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthis close in on Bab el-Mandeb as Brent barrel price soars to over $106</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f67151bfdfd19d3d5c6e6619819b06eaaa3ad92cc2df23287bf75a54a4ab25f</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T02:46:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain--16e2d74b863a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthis on Thursday gained further leverage over the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, one of the world's most critical shipping routes amid the ongoing blockade of the Strait of Hormuz. Meanwhile, price for Brent crude oil soared more than 5 percent to over $106 per barrel. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran and US strike tankers in biggest shipping attack since war began</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b79619edce8e483a807870fe0e89efeadd85d5b67f8ff14e33b57ffc76ed70d</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T20:31:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260909-iran-and-us-strike-tankers-in-biggest-shipping-attack-since-war-began--4d2b3cd0d7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260909-iran-and-us-strike-tankers-in-biggest-shipping-attack-since-war-began" /><summary type="html">Iran and the US on Wednesday traded their biggest wave of attacks on shipping since the war began, with Iran saying it struck 10 vessels near the Strait of Hormuz after US forces sank five Iranian oil tankers. Brent crude oil surged above $100 a barrel as fears grew over global energy supplies.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi offensive on Bab al-Mandeb may bring 'tremendous leverage', analyst explains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5de9d4239a4e4381ae990dda873b84974238492f357639f942a971fd76cb4592</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:35:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/houthi-offensive-on-bab-al-mandeb-may-bring-tremendous-leverage-analyst-explains--fe459ea32af6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-offensive-on-bab-al-mandeb-may-bring-tremendous-leverage-analyst-explains" /><summary type="html">The Saudi-led coalition in Yemen on Wednesday said the Iran-backed Houthis had launched fresh attacks on the kingdom's south, after the rebels launched an offensive seeking to control the Bab al-Mandab Strait. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Adam Baron, Fellow at the New America Foundation, says that "if you have both groups able to disrupt maritime shipping both in the Red Sea and the Gulf, this would be a tremendous exercise of leverage to put pressure for a resolution".</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran strikes ships, expands no-go zone outside Hormuz strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dcdfb1623a1e982758811557c82750729152ad2c20ae164fdf74c4c7436b94c</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T18:30:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-strikes-ships-expands-no-go-zone-outside-hormuz-strait--ad14b4ac2e24.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-strikes-ships-expands-no-go-zone-outside-hormuz-strait" /><summary type="html">Iran said it attacked more than a dozen vessels trying to pass through the Strait of Hormuz on Wednesday, as it announced an expansion of a no-go zone outside the strategic waterway it has blockaded for months. The fresh attacks and fighting with the United States have sent oil prices above $100 per barrel again as Tehran chokes off the strait and Washington presses a counter-blockade of Iranian ports. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>The Times: 'Counterproductive' sanctions on Israel don't match the 'theatrical rhetoric'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1a8caa61c58c81c11ba28d56fb4c64051cc6ab3be852bf083df9f3a4dd8bfc0</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:35:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260909-the-times-counterproductive-sanctions-on-israel-don-t-match-the-theatrical-rhetoric--24a57d7cc6c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260909-the-times-counterproductive-sanctions-on-israel-don-t-match-the-theatrical-rhetoric" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, September 9: British papers are reacting to the sanctions imposed on Israel. Next: Israeli papers discuss Haaretz's October 7 revelatory investigation. Also: CDs are back! Finally, South Park renames itself to South America to mock Trump.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>'New escalation in Yemen deeply concerning everyone in the region'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:265305d68450518a70f2bda8f8fdacf54cbe344f5d7835911d3d77a25c77f8ab</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T10:39:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/new-escalation-in-yemen-deeply-concerning-everyone-in-the-region--833547815e7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/new-escalation-in-yemen-deeply-concerning-everyone-in-the-region" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Jules Grange Gastinel, Researcher at the Institute for Research and Studies on the Arab and Muslim World (IREMAM). He depicts Yemen as moving from a prolonged condition of unresolved conflict into renewed regional confrontation. The relative calm established after 2022, he argues, never amounted to a durable political settlement: Yemen remains divided between rival political, financial and military institutions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel gives UK 30 days to close consulate in Jerusalem</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99b23bec5d4d1c1fde7c96c4fe627b0d18a9b7359d3c1eae5276be4e280d2899</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T23:07:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-us-destroys-five-iranian-oil-tankers-as-iran-threatens-kuwait-and-bahrain--06fb925ebc76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-us-destroys-five-iranian-oil-tankers-as-iran-threatens-kuwait-and-bahrain" /><summary type="html">Israel has given Britain 30 days to close its east Jerusalem consulate in response to UK sanctions on goods from Israeli settlements, a move Prime Minister Andy Burnham defended Wednesday as necessary to “stand against injustice” in the occupied West Bank. The UK, France and Canada on Tuesday joined nine other European countries imposing the trade ban. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UK, France, ⁠Canada sanction Israeli West Bank goods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19a33fcfaafa04d61b338f54f487ae05d95c8477dade50410d407392169e6208</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T21:02:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260908-uk-france-canada-sanction-israeli-west-bank-goods--fdacae129b44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260908-uk-france-canada-sanction-israeli-west-bank-goods" /><summary type="html">Israel said on Tuesday it was closing Britain's consulate in East Jerusalem in response to plans by the UK, France and Canada to block imports from Israeli settlements in the West Bank. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Julie Norman, Associate Fellow with the Middle East and North Africa Programme at Chatham House and Director of University College London’s Israel-Palestine Initiative.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu under fire over report UAE warned of October 7 attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6d992914c019533b2ce76a2eb7d02759b92f5497d689a9bf6ba0058c9f44db6</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:31:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-under-fire-over-report-uae-warned-of-october-7-attack--7fd6213c811c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-under-fire-over-report-uae-warned-of-october-7-attack" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leaders on Tuesday called Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu unfit to serve after a report that the United Arab Emirates had warned him before the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack. Haaretz newspaper, in a report excerpted from a forthcoming book by its reporters, said UAE President Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan spoke to Netanyahu a week and a half before the attack and told him that Hamas was planning a major operation. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK, France, Canada to ban imports from Israeli settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15e56af5c4be8ee5fe8eedff06b2a7e763dbd20a870caf7b3b57f8832ba74d82</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:24:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-france-canada-to-ban-imports-from-israeli-settlements--5103789d99a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-france-canada-to-ban-imports-from-israeli-settlements" /><summary type="html">Britain, France and Canada said Tuesday they will ban imports from Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank, with a UK minister accusing Israel of turning a blind eye to the "ethnic cleansing" of Palestinians there. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fc69536b64c4f6308b73d0c7024605eb1d31a410117fcf384d3ec0e56bb5b45</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:16:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war--1e3a59faed45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel to close British consulate in Jerusalem after sanctions on settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66595961144ff6edc6781caef957b3446c943914b94fa62931e87bf0d08c7b67</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T15:10:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-israel-to-close-british-consulate-in-jerusalem-after-sanctions-on-settleme--6854a83facb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-israel-to-close-british-consulate-in-jerusalem-after-sanctions-on-settlements" /><summary type="html">British Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband accused the Israeli government on Tuesday of turning a "blind eye" to what he called "ethnic cleansing" by settlers in the West Bank as the UK joined France and ten other countries in banning imports from Israeli settlements in the occupied territory. The decision comes amid rising violence over settlement expansion. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>France, UK to join 10 other countries in banning goods from Israeli West Bank settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ed43722e85a2bb33373b7d8d47f72513a4f8e8c35195c696b849286cb2a2e34</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:54:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-france-and-canada-to-join-uk-in-banning-goods-from-israeli-west-bank-settlements--b760488b9f5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-france-and-canada-to-join-uk-in-banning-goods-from-israeli-west-bank-settlements" /><summary type="html">France is preparing to introduce a ban on products from Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël ​Barrot said on Tuesday, following a wave of settler violence in recent days that has further undermined prospects for a two-state solution with the Palestinians. France has joined the UK and ten other countries in announcing the trade ban on goods, and some services, from Israeli settlements.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UAE leader warned Netanyahu of Hamas attack days before October 7, says report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b85326f31be17dc09fb67ff9f022263c31dc01efcb69dd0570082abe38cf14</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:40:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-uae-leader-warned-netanyahu-of-hamas-attack-days-before-october-7-says-report--a3829f73dcb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-uae-leader-warned-netanyahu-of-hamas-attack-days-before-october-7-says-report" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu faced strong backlash from opposition leaders on Tuesday after a report published by Haaretz newspaper said UAE President Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan warned Netanyahu that Hamas was planning a major operation days before the attacks on October 7. The report alleges that Netanyahu failed to inform security chiefs.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks disrupt Saudi oil facilities and wound more than 70</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e67904e3ebc65dc137dc74a649a152124918e0740246ea4454b831ef2bfe7c7</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:14:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-houthi-attacks-disrupt-saudi-oil-facilities-and-wound-more-than-70--ed16b49517da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-houthi-attacks-disrupt-saudi-oil-facilities-and-wound-more-than-70" /><summary type="html">Houthi forces attacked four cities in southern Saudi Arabia on Tuesday, wounding at least 73 people and setting oil facilities ablaze in one of the largest assaults on the US ally since the wider Gulf war began. The strikes came as explosions were reported at Iran’s Kharg Island and the Gulf of Oman port of ​Jask, raising fears of renewed US attacks and further escalation.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel intensifies south Lebanon strikes, killing 13 after weeks-long lull</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:653a3d98049f5867b3dc7f22d5a8a7110ac64eef5416f4ac6cd909feb9ead238</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T21:32:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israeli-strikes-south-lebanon-violence--1ad7641e3826.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israeli-strikes-south-lebanon-violence" /><summary type="html">Israel launched a wave of air strikes across southern Lebanon, killing 13 people, including women and children, Lebanon’s health ministry said on Monday, marking an escalation after weeks of relative calm. Israel said it would continue targeting Iran-backed Hezbollah over alleged ceasefire violations. Hezbollah has not commented on the strikes.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel warns of 'full-scale war' if Palestinian Authority launches Oct. 7-style attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3880871c6129618d158bd3cfd9131041c07b5c1decf2d2deef04db57a5f9f979</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:08:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israel-warns-of-full-scale-war-if-palestinian-authority-launches-oct-7-style-attack--e5884b7104de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israel-warns-of-full-scale-war-if-palestinian-authority-launches-oct-7-style-attack" /><summary type="html">Israel on Monday threatened a “full-scale war” against the Palestinian Authority if it believed the West Bank-based body was preparing an attack on Israeli forces or settlements resembling Hamas’s October 7, 2023 assault. The warning was denounced by Palestinian authorities as an attempt to fuel the conflict during the Israeli election season.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon kill 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f587cbef30a999f318245b1359326c960432d81cce0d8db561dc771f85761d0e</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:10:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-israeli-strikes-on-southern-lebanon-kill-11--4d2222e87b6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-israeli-strikes-on-southern-lebanon-kill-11" /><summary type="html">Israeli strikes ⁠on a ​southern Lebanese town early on Monday killed at least 11 people including two children ​and two medics, Lebanon's state news agency said. Israel has intensified its bombardment of south Lebanon in recent days despite a June ceasefire that was meant ​to halt fighting ‌between the Israeli military and Lebanese armed ⁠group Hezbollah.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN rapporteur says Israeli rubble-clearing in Gaza could erase 'atrocity crimes' evidence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:003f17360050be467662f683ffe732c760edeca598abcbeb0d9083a74a049f46</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:51:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-un-rapporteur-says-israeli-rubble-clearing-in-gaza-could-erase-atrocity-crimes-evidence--bf0ebb6f2138.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-un-rapporteur-says-israeli-rubble-clearing-in-gaza-could-erase-atrocity-crimes-evidence" /><summary type="html">The United Nations Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese warned on Monday that the large-scale rubble removal in parts of Gaza under Israeli control could risk erasing "evidence relevant to the investigation of alleged international crimes".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Several killed in Israeli strikes in southern Lebanon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fb1665abbad1677011420da3fdce9cdd5898248083373a6a33eae616d302945</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T01:13:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-middle-east-live-israel-army-orders-evacuation-of-zone-in-south-lebanon-ahead-of-strikes--2806097dc20d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-middle-east-live-israel-army-orders-evacuation-of-zone-in-south-lebanon-ahead-of-strikes" /><summary type="html">At ⁠least ​11 ​people were killed, including two infants, were injured ⁠in Israeli strikes on ​a ‌residential building in ‌a town ​in southern Lebanon early on Monday, ​Lebanon's ​state ​news agency ​reported. The Israeli army had demanded early Monday that residents of Deir Zahrani in southern Lebanon leave a specific zone ahead of strikes against Iran-backed Hezbollah. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
